{"name":"Second Pour","hex":"#887ca4","fetched":"2026-10-13","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"second","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Number-two; following after the first one with nothing between them. The ordinal number corresponding to the cardinal number two.","Next to the first in value, power, excellence, dignity, or rank; secondary; subordinate; inferior."]},{"part":"Adverb","definitions":["After the first; at the second rank.","After the first occurrence but before the third."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/second"},{"term":"pour","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To cause (liquid, or liquid-like substance) to flow in a stream, either out of a container or into it.","To send out as in a stream or a flood; to cause (an emotion) to come out; to cause to escape."]},{"part":"Noun","definitions":["The act of pouring.","Something, or an amount, poured."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/pour"}],"entries":[{"title":"Second","blocks":[{"text":"The second is a unit of time derived from the division of the day, first into 24 hours, then into 60 minutes, and lastly into 60 seconds, for a total of 24 × 60 × 60 = 86400 seconds per day. That definition, based on 1⁄86400 of a rotation of the Earth, is still used by the Universal Time 1 (UT1) system."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/15/Clock-pendulum.gif/330px-Clock-pendulum.gif?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Second"}],"images":[],"sounds":{"second":[{"type":"audio/ogg; codecs=\"vorbis\"","src":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/9/9f/En-us-2nd.ogg?utm_source=en.wiktionary.org&utm_campaign=rest&utm_content=original"},{"type":"audio/mpeg","src":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/transcoded/9/9f/En-us-2nd.ogg/En-us-2nd.ogg.mp3"},{"type":"audio/ogg; codecs=\"vorbis\"","src":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/e/eb/En-u